WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:06.490
The Joe Biden administration has already done
so much that I want to spend time today focusing

00:00:06.490 --> 00:00:12.610
on that, but we should talk about the inauguration,
which happened yesterday, it was notable in

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:16.690
that it was very different than past inaugurations
for a number of reasons.

00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:18.950
It took place during a global hundred year
pandemic.

00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:24.390
And so the crowd was very, very small and
the entire National Mall, which would often

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:28.810
be filled with people to different degrees,
depending on which inauguration we're talking

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:29.810
about.

00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:33.950
As we know, the crowd size of inaugurations
has been a flashpoint in the past, empty with

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:34.960
flags.

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:39.770
Instead, the outgoing president wasn't there
for the first time in 152 years.

00:00:39.770 --> 00:00:44.450
Donald Trump fleeing Washington, D.C. for
Palm Beach, Florida, early in the morning

00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:45.450
yesterday.

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:47.219
But Joe Biden was sworn in.

00:00:47.219 --> 00:00:49.090
There were no incidents of violence.

00:00:49.090 --> 00:00:54.160
There were no arrests or unrest in the area,
just the new presidency.

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:58.280
And Vice President Kamala Harris being sworn
in here.

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:03.610
Supreme Court Justice Sonia Sotomayor does
mispronounce Carmela's name as Kamala.

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:04.610
No one's perfect.

00:01:04.610 --> 00:01:07.869
I expect that there will be much of that in
the next few years.

00:01:07.869 --> 00:01:12.459
Please raise your right hand and repeat after
me.

00:01:12.459 --> 00:01:16.270
I, Kamala Harris, do solemnly swear.

00:01:16.270 --> 00:01:22.349
I, Kamala Harris, solemnly swear that I will
support and defend the Constitution of the

00:01:22.349 --> 00:01:27.959
United States, that I will support and defend
the Constitution against all enemies, foreign

00:01:27.959 --> 00:01:33.999
and domestic, against all enemies, foreign
and domestic, that I will bear true faith

00:01:33.999 --> 00:01:39.085
and allegiance to the same, that I will bear
true faith and allegiance.

00:01:39.085 --> 00:01:44.329
That I take this obligation freely, that I
take this obligation freely without any mental

00:01:44.329 --> 00:01:50.069
reservation or purpose of evasion, without
any mental reservation or purpose of evasion,

00:01:50.069 --> 00:01:54.609
that I will well and faithfully discharge,
that I will well and faithfully discharge

00:01:54.609 --> 00:01:59.789
the duties of the office on which I am about
to enter the duties of the office upon which

00:01:59.789 --> 00:02:01.329
I am about to enter.

00:02:01.329 --> 00:02:03.329
So help me God.

00:02:03.329 --> 00:02:05.539
So help me God.

00:02:05.539 --> 00:02:12.610
And then Joe Biden also sworn in by the chief
justice of the Supreme Court, John Roberts,

00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:15.850
please raise your right hand and repeat after
me.

00:02:15.850 --> 00:02:20.390
I, Joseph Robinette Biden Jr., do solemnly
swear.

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:26.019
Joseph Robinette Biden Jr. do solemnly swear
that I will faithfully execute, that I will

00:02:26.019 --> 00:02:31.030
faithfully execute the office of president
of the United States, office of president

00:02:31.030 --> 00:02:32.280
of the United States.

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:37.489
And will, to the best of my ability, well,
to the best of my ability, preserve, protect

00:02:37.489 --> 00:02:43.480
and defend, preserve, protect and defend the
Constitution of the United States Constitution

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:44.530
of the United States.

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:45.579
So help you God.

00:02:45.579 --> 00:02:51.049
So help me God.

00:02:51.049 --> 00:03:06.180
Congratulations, Mr. President.

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:13.170
So there it is, Trump out, Biden in Biden
giving a speech focused on unity, the the

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:20.079
the pragmatic reality is there will likely
not be the unity Biden calls for, but Biden

00:03:20.079 --> 00:03:24.700
calling for it, not mentioning Trump once,
but mentioning the big challenges that lie

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:30.870
ahead of the country for the country, including
starting to be respected again by the world,

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:33.249
dealing with the virus and more.

00:03:33.249 --> 00:03:35.700
Here is Joe Biden talking about that.

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:42.299
I know, speaking of unity, can sound to some
like a foolish fantasy these days.

00:03:42.299 --> 00:03:50.010
I know the forces that divide us are deep
and they are real, but I also know they are

00:03:50.010 --> 00:03:51.890
not new.

00:03:51.890 --> 00:03:58.349
Our history has been a constant struggle between
the American ideal that we are all are created

00:03:58.349 --> 00:04:09.370
equal and the harsh, ugly reality that racism,
nativism, fear, demonization have long torn

00:04:09.370 --> 00:04:10.650
us apart.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:18.090
Biden directly attacking the deceptive and
pernicious disinformation that has become

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:27.449
standard during Trump in America, about which
during which we saw facts manufactured.

00:04:27.449 --> 00:04:35.620
Every disagreement doesn't have to be a cause
for total war, and we must reject the culture

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:43.190
in which facts themselves are manipulated
and even manufactured.

00:04:43.190 --> 00:04:52.280
Now, former Vice President Mike Pence at the
inauguration not clapping on that one and

00:04:52.280 --> 00:04:54.509
during many others, and why would he?

00:04:54.509 --> 00:04:59.630
Biden is pointing directly to him, not with
his finger, but with his words.

00:04:59.630 --> 00:05:05.229
And it is Pence and Trump and their supporters
and media allies that did the manufacturing

00:05:05.229 --> 00:05:07.849
of many of those so-called facts.

00:05:07.849 --> 00:05:14.540
Joe Biden then telling the folks that did
not support him, that he will also be their

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:21.000
president and asking them to hear him out.

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:27.050
All those who supported our campaign, I'm
humbled by the faith you've placed in us to

00:05:27.050 --> 00:05:28.710
all those who did not support us.

00:05:28.710 --> 00:05:31.300
Let me say this.

00:05:31.300 --> 00:05:34.060
Hear me out as we move forward.

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:36.099
Take a measure of me and my heart.

00:05:36.099 --> 00:05:40.039
If you still disagree, so be it.

00:05:40.039 --> 00:05:41.220
That's democracy.

00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:43.340
That's America.

00:05:43.340 --> 00:05:49.620
The right to dissent peaceably in the guardrails
of our republic is perhaps this nation's greatest

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:51.330
strength.

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:57.210
Yet here we clearly disagreement must not
lead to this union.

00:05:57.210 --> 00:05:59.200
And I pledge this to you.

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:04.380
I will be a president for all Americans, all
Americans.

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:07.870
And then Joe Biden saying we will repair our
alliances.

00:06:07.870 --> 00:06:12.960
Of course, the reason these alliances need
repair is that they were destroyed by the

00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:14.320
Trump administration.

00:06:14.320 --> 00:06:20.130
Biden doesn't say that, but it's certainly
implied.

00:06:20.130 --> 00:06:28.700
We all understand the world is watching, watching
all of us today, so here's my message to those

00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:31.720
beyond our borders.

00:06:31.720 --> 00:06:36.979
America has been tested and we've come out
stronger for it.

00:06:36.979 --> 00:06:43.659
We will repair our alliances and engage with
the world once again, not to be yesterday's

00:06:43.659 --> 00:06:47.659
challenges, but today's and tomorrow's challenges.

00:06:47.659 --> 00:06:50.530
So this was the right speech for the right
moment.

00:06:50.530 --> 00:06:57.229
And very quickly, I mean, almost instantly,
in a sense, we shifted from the ceremonial

00:06:57.229 --> 00:07:00.050
to the logistical and to getting things done.

00:07:00.050 --> 00:07:05.680
There are so many things desperately needed
and shockingly overdue right now that there's

00:07:05.680 --> 00:07:13.919
quite literally no time to bask in the afterglow
of the inauguration and the afterglow of the

00:07:13.919 --> 00:07:18.710
fireworks, the literal afterglow, because
there's so much that needs to get done.

00:07:18.710 --> 00:08:30.569
And that's exactly what I want to talk about
next.

